{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list","id":1546508,"title":"Next on the Technocracy's Hit List...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-30T19:47:45-08:00","id":1546508,"title":"Next on the Technocracy's Hit List...","content":"The Scenario: The Technocracy has finally WON the Ascension War, definitively! The Council and Disparates are shattered, most of the survivors being taken out or brainwashed; the Marauders and Nephandi have been purged from Creation and chased back out of Reality; and the Crafts are hiding, hoping to avoid notice. After a period of regrouping, replenishing membership and repair, the Order of Reason is stronger than ever!<br /> <br /> The Inner Circle decides it's finally time to advance the Time Table and move on to wiping out the rest of the Reality Deviants corrupting the Tellurian. But...where to start?<br /> <br /> YOU are now pulling the strings of the Technocracy! All its resources are at your command...Who do you send them after first? The vampires who infest the bureaucracies of the cities? The Werecreatures who stalk the wilderness? The ghosts who haunt the living? The Fae who eat their dreams? <br /> <br /> And HOW will you do it? What strategies will you use to best take out your targets? What will you do if they prove tougher than you thought, and somehow turn the tides against you? The Consensus is waiting for YOU to decide!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T09:53:20-08:00","id":1546648,"title":"","content":"With these crossovers, I have a few considerations.<br /> <br /> First, the Nefandi are near extinct. Does this mean that the other splats &quot;nefandi-like&quot; were also driven out?<br /> <br /> I ask because that would have to mean that the Wyrm agents the Were-beasts fight have also been driven back into the hole from which they came.<br /> <br /> If that is the case, then my next target would be the Were-beasts. Because they would be free to antagonize the Union, and they absolutely would be unfriendly to it.<br /> <br /> Vampires are a nuisance, but they actually clean up for their own. They are undeniably a threat, however they are funnily enough the splat with less risk of ruining things for the Union, given their so adamant &quot;maskerade&quot; doctrine. They are also very hard to put out of their holes, being experts into hiding. I would therefore place them at the bottom of problems to deal with after all others have been resolved.<br /> <br /> The Ghosts also have a policy of not messing with the living; besides, there's literally MILLIONS of them. A real herculean feat, which I don't consider feasible or desirable, unless the Union becomes so massively powerful that anything else is like bugs in comparison, but then such considerations would be unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I might be tempt to put the Changelings first, but only because they are probably the least dangerous of them all, thus I would use the Union's might to swiftly deal with it and have one less problem to deal with, before getting embroiled in more resource draining wars with other foes.<br /> <br /> But definitely, the Were-beasts would be an ideal target, as the first ones to go or after the Fae. And the way to do it would be similar (but not identical) to how the Wyrm agents fight them. Taking their Caerns is ideal for the Union, because it both weakens them while also strengthen the Union.<br /> <br /> With the Wyrm basically defeated thou, having the Void Engineers manage to direct several &quot;dimensional Stasis entities&quot; (call them &quot;Weaver Spirits&quot; if you will) would be a solid strategy.<br /> <br /> Then, at the level of the Masses, unleashing anti-environmentalist propaganda would also be massively effective.<br /> <br /> Now, if these prove to be a nut too tough to crack, then the Union's only options would be diplomacy, subversion or giving up.<br /> <br /> Diplomacy would involve trying to go to a settlement. Easy down on your bio-terrorism, and we will easy down on the Progrom. As both sides realize the costs of such a war, it could actually be feasible.<br /> <br /> Subversion implies trying to involve the other splats on the fight, not necessarily in favor of the Union, but it would be sufficient to have them against the Were-beasts. No actual garantees here that it would work, but it's worth a shot. This could actually succeed, because the Weres aren't the most diplomatic of the splats, but it has it's own risks and problems.<br /> <br /> Giving up actually means to retreat from the all out war, saving resources and reassessing things in order to try again in the future. Thus, instead of an active full force Pogrom, the Union recedes, go into defense to protect it's assets, let things cool up and live to fight another day rather than burning itself up into a futile crusade. Then, rather then going full berserk to exterminate the enemy as initially planned, it's back to &quot;contention mode&quot; as it has always been doing, with small punctual actions rather than major global mobilization","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T05:50:45-08:00","id":1546862,"title":"","content":"Assuming that they still exist and are a problem, I would go after various servants of the Wyrm - primarily Pentex and their allies.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy will be guiding the government and corporations, not a bunch of demon worshipping doomsday cultists.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll round up all of the big shots in Pentex and kill or imprison them. We\u2019ll break up the various companies. We\u2019ll purge the factories and power plants of any banes or other Wyrm tainted evilness. <br /> <br /> Maybe even more important in opposing the Pentex agenda - we will clean up industry and the environment. We can release new clean energy to the masses, make industry less polluting and more energy efficient. We will use renewable resources. The vision of the future will be purged of this particular downside of industrialization. <br /> <br /> That will stop the Wyrm agenda.<br /> <br /> Ironically, this stuff would help werewolves, though they may be next on my chopping block after combating the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T13:14:11-08:00","id":1546874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list?p=1546862#post1546862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that they still exist and are a problem, I would go after various servants of the Wyrm - primarily Pentex and their allies.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy will be guiding the government and corporations, not a bunch of demon worshipping doomsday cultists.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll round up all of the big shots in Pentex and kill or imprison them. We\u2019ll break up the various companies. We\u2019ll purge the factories and power plants of any banes or other Wyrm tainted evilness.<br /> <br /> Maybe even more important in opposing the Pentex agenda - we will clean up industry and the environment. We can release new clean energy to the masses, make industry less polluting and more energy efficient. We will use renewable resources. The vision of the future will be purged of this particular downside of industrialization.<br /> <br /> That will stop the Wyrm agenda.<br /> <br /> Ironically, this stuff would help werewolves, though they may be next on my chopping block after combating the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, since OP mentioned that the Nefandi were else defeated, I assumed that so too would the Wyrm minions be.<br /> <br /> In case the Wyrm is still around and kicking, then it's obviously it that would be the target.<br /> <br /> Then, the Beast folk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T14:16:46-08:00","id":1546876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list?p=1546874#post1546874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, since OP mentioned that the Nefandi were else defeated, I assumed that so too would the Wyrm minions be.<br /> <br /> In case the Wyrm is still around and kicking, then it's obviously it that would be the io<br /> <br /> Then, the Beast folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think we\u2019re on the same page here. It depends on what Wyrm minions are left. If their threat is neutralized, then Garou and other shifters should be taken down I. If we still have the Wyrm, we go it after it as well as Pentex,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T18:13:20-08:00","id":1547014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list?p=1546876#post1546876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I think we\u2019re on the same page here. It depends on what Wyrm minions are left. If their threat is neutralized, then Garou and other shifters should be taken down I. If we still have the Wyrm, we go it after it as well as Pentex,</div> </div> </div> </div>Their threat won't be neutralized by the Technocracy. The TU supports the underlying issues that make Pentex possible in the first place, and it's far from the only Wyrm-influenced corporation (WIC) out there. The Union could be busy trying to play whack a mole with WICs for decades or centuries and never manage to do much of anything, even if it doesn't get subverted by agents of the Defiler Triatic Wyrm, which are exceedingly accomplished and well-practiced at riding the Weaver's webs down to taint whatever can be found stuck to them.<br /> <br /> But they'd get subverted way before that. The self-righteous bastards would never see it coming due to their blind spots. They'd trip and fall into <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3LKadZ4LFU\" target=\"_blank\">Repercussions of Evil</a>, over and over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T13:05:00-08:00","id":1547035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list?p=1547014#post1547014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Their threat won't be neutralized by the Technocracy. The TU supports the underlying issues that make Pentex possible in the first place, and it's far from the only Wyrm-influenced corporation (WIC) out there. The Union could be busy trying to play whack a mole with WICs for decades or centuries and never manage to do much of anything, even if it doesn't get subverted by agents of the Defiler Triatic Wyrm, which are exceedingly accomplished and well-practiced at riding the Weaver's webs down to taint whatever can be found stuck to them.<br /> <br /> But they'd get subverted way before that. The self-righteous bastards would never see it coming due to their blind spots. They'd trip and fall into <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3LKadZ4LFU\" target=\"_blank\">Repercussions of Evil</a>, over and over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is a highly unlikely scenario, much like as the Sabbath being completely wiped out by the Camarilla or the Garou Nation actually succeeding against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> But that was the premise of OP, that the Traditions were gone for good and the nefandic forces too - which I then asked if that meant that Wyrm agents were out of the picture as well, IN WHICH CASE then the next target would be the Werebeasts, however, if the Wyrm is still around (well, its agents obviously, because the Wyrm will always be around), then the Techies would divert their resources to that threat. And yes, ithey would take perhaps centuries in that shadow war against it, with no garantees of victory - but neither would it be a doomed battle as in the case for the Garou.<br /> <br /> But the original premise is that the Wyrm agents are gone and restricted to their hellholes at the Umbra, which includes the Pentex and all others - assume therefore that project Invictus was massively successful, the NWO managed to root out the Pentex corruption from the Syndicate and they did it without fracturing the Union in the process and so on. Again, highly unlikely, but that's the established premise we're working with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T23:31:09-08:00","id":1547049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list?p=1547035#post1547035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it is a highly unlikely scenario, much like as the Sabbath being completely wiped out by the Camarilla or the Garou Nation actually succeeding against the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a rather vast gulf separating those two examples, just to be clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that was the premise of OP, that the Traditions were gone for good and the nefandic forces too - which I then asked if that meant that Wyrm agents were out of the picture as well, IN WHICH CASE then the next target would be the Werebeasts, however, if the Wyrm is still around (well, its agents obviously, because the Wyrm will always be around), then the Techies would divert their resources to that threat. And yes, ithey would take perhaps centuries in that shadow war against it, with no garantees of victory - but neither would it be a doomed battle as in the case for the Garou. </div> </div> </div>How would getting rid of the Nephandi get rid of all things touched by corruption? It would only get rid of one faction of corrupt beings. The askew nature of the universe remains. Also, yes, it would be a doomed battle. Anything that's not a successful use of that one rite at the end of Weaver Ascendant just resets the clock - and the Union doesn't know about it. They'll have numerous conjectures about the nature of their enemy, all of them highly biased and wrong in a manner that even D.N.A. would scratch their heads at and say &quot;I think you've overlooked something here.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the original premise is that the Wyrm agents are gone and restricted to their hellholes at the Umbra, which includes the Pentex and all others - assume therefore that project Invictus was massively successful, the NWO managed to root out the Pentex corruption from the Syndicate and they did it without fracturing the Union in the process and so on. Again, highly unlikely, but that's the established premise we're working with </div> </div> </div>Beyond highly unlikely, again, as in the rather vast gulf that started this post. The Sabbat are just a bunch of more self-indulgent vampires that like to cosplay a cult. Fractured forces of the cosmos whose worries and dissociative identities become supergods are something else entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T02:48:10-08:00","id":1547050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list?p=1547049#post1547049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a rather vast gulf separating those two examples, just to be clear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How would getting rid of the Nephandi get rid of all things touched by corruption? It would only get rid of one faction of corrupt beings. The askew nature of the universe remains. Also, yes, it would be a doomed battle. Anything that's not a successful use of that one rite at the end of Weaver Ascendant just resets the clock - and the Union doesn't know about it. They'll have numerous conjectures about the nature of their enemy, all of them highly biased and wrong in a manner that even D.N.A. would scratch their heads at and say &quot;I think you've overlooked something here.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Beyond highly unlikely, again, as in the rather vast gulf that started this post. The Sabbat are just a bunch of more self-indulgent vampires that like to cosplay a cult. Fractured forces of the cosmos whose worries and dissociative identities become supergods are something else entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that technically, &quot;Nefandi&quot; could mean just a single &quot;faction&quot; of corruption, it could just mean awakened fallen Mages, but in Mage terminology it actually embarks ALL corrupt elements. Thus, to say that &quot;the Nefandi are defeated&quot; implies that ALL corruption is driven away - not destroyed and vanquished, but rather driven away, back from the holes they sprung from.<br /> <br /> I know it is a rather preposterous proposition, but it is the presumption we are to ponder upon at priori. And if I continue with that same phrasing format I'll soon write a rap song.<br /> <br /> Sure, the Sabbath doesn't compare to the Wyrm. That was not the intent to make it look like it so. Nevertheless, it doesn't matter how unlikely the situation it is, we are to assume it that way at priori as already ascertained above and damn, the rap gods must be trying to possess me today for some inscrutable reason","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T08:45:06-08:00","id":1547059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list?p=1547050#post1547050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand that technically, &quot;Nefandi&quot; could mean just a single &quot;faction&quot; of corruption, it could just mean awakened fallen Mages, but in Mage terminology it actually embarks ALL corrupt elements. Thus, to say that &quot;the Nefandi are defeated&quot; implies that ALL corruption is driven away - not destroyed and vanquished, but rather driven away, back from the holes they sprung from.<br /> <br /> I know it is a rather preposterous proposition, but it is the presumption we are to ponder upon at priori. And if I continue with that same phrasing format I'll soon write a rap song.<br /> <br /> Sure, the Sabbath doesn't compare to the Wyrm. That was not the intent to make it look like it so. Nevertheless, it doesn't matter how unlikely the situation it is, we are to assume it that way at priori as already ascertained above and damn, the rap gods must be trying to possess me today for some inscrutable reason</div> </div> </div> </div>You asserted it, OP didn't. We're not bound to accept the assertion, since it doesn't hold up in the apparent crossover environment that results. Else, you're not playing with the actual other games, you're playing with Mage's funhouse distortions of them, and since this thread is on the general WoD board and not the Mage board specifically, I'd reject that premise as being far, far too Mage for the challenges that this premise anticipates ahead of the TU. Even in Mage, one could surmise that the TU gutting the rest of the willworker population causes the importance of the consensus to fall apart, replacing what used to be Mage with bits of other games as if it had always been that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T21:01:23-08:00","id":1547089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list?p=1547059#post1547059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You asserted it, OP didn't. We're not bound to accept the assertion, since it doesn't hold up in the apparent crossover environment that results. Else, you're not playing with the actual other games, you're playing with Mage's funhouse distortions of them, and since this thread is on the general WoD board and not the Mage board specifically, I'd reject that premise as being far, far too Mage for the challenges that this premise anticipates ahead of the TU. Even in Mage, one could surmise that the TU gutting the rest of the willworker population causes the importance of the consensus to fall apart, replacing what used to be Mage with bits of other games as if it had always been that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I asked if the Wyrm was included in the chopping blocks; it doesn't matter if it is MtA or crossover, &quot;Nephandi&quot; is a terminology that is used in MtA, and it relies on ALL corrupt forces of the Tellurian. &quot;Nephandi&quot; doesn't come from Vampire, nor WtA nor Mummy or Changeling. It comes from Mage. While you can make distinctions (there are the infernalists, there are the Wyrm cultists and there are the Cthulhesque things from the outside), that still doesn't change from the fact that the term &quot;Nephandi&quot; embarks ALL corruption.<br /> <br /> You could change the word &quot;Nephandi&quot; for &quot;all the sources of corruption in the Tellurian&quot;, and it would retain its meaning.<br /> <br /> Other than that, then you would have to be discussing semantics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T21:26:28-08:00","id":1547092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list?p=1547089#post1547089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I asked if the Wyrm was included in the chopping blocks; it doesn't matter if it is MtA or crossover, &quot;Nephandi&quot; is a terminology that is used in MtA, and it relies on ALL corrupt forces of the Tellurian. &quot;Nephandi&quot; doesn't come from Vampire, nor WtA nor Mummy or Changeling. It comes from Mage. While you can make distinctions (there are the infernalists, there are the Wyrm cultists and there are the Cthulhesque things from the outside), that still doesn't change from the fact that the term &quot;Nephandi&quot; embarks ALL corruption.<br /> <br /> You could change the word &quot;Nephandi&quot; for &quot;all the sources of corruption in the Tellurian&quot;, and it would retain its meaning.<br /> <br /> Other than that, then you would have to be discussing semantics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when? M20 first and foremost uses it to describe mages, specifically, who follow the Path of Descent. If it's talking about their patrons, then it refers to something like the Outer Darkness, which are distinct from the fallen mages themselves. Non-mages aren't really a part of the structure, it seems, as they're referred to as pawns, and likely refer to cast-offs of other games' antagonists that pal around them or act as mercenaries rather than pursuing their respective setting's organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T16:53:24-08:00","id":1547120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list?p=1547092#post1547092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since when? M20 first and foremost uses it to describe mages, specifically, who follow the Path of Descent. If it's talking about their patrons, then it refers to something like the Outer Darkness, which are distinct from the fallen mages themselves. Non-mages aren't really a part of the structure, it seems, as they're referred to as pawns, and likely refer to cast-offs of other games' antagonists that pal around them or act as mercenaries rather than pursuing their respective setting's organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can mean both. &quot;Nephandi&quot; yes, it is used to describe the fallen Awaken. But it can also be used to describe the collective forces of corruption. It has been used to describe that on several occasions. I'll admit that M20 is the one I have least memory of, I read it once but I don't mind using it all too much, since the only thing I really need the books for is to look up some Spheres or the eventual rule, and even that is rare, since I know most of them by memory. But I can tell you that this is used extensively from the 1st Ed to rev, and even in the Sorcerers' Crusade and other supplements. &quot;Nephandi&quot; can be used to talk about the fallen Mages but also about ALL forces of corruption (that is, the Fallens' pawns and also their masters). The way to distinguish between each use is a matter of context. If memory serves, even books that talk about the fallen (like the &quot;Book of Madness&quot; for example) uses the term Nephandi with BOTH meanings - sometimes referring just to the fallen mages, sometimes referring to all forces of corruption, with the difference being left exclusively to the context.<br /> <br /> Granted, I see now how this creates more confusion than it solves, but that's how it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-18T10:52:20-08:00","id":1547131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list?p=1547120#post1547120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can mean both. &quot;Nephandi&quot; yes, it is used to describe the fallen Awaken. But it can also be used to describe the collective forces of corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in Mage, and only for Mage-specific corrupt groups headed up and staffed mostly by Mages and sorcerers. Outside of Mage, it's just not going to get used, because BSDs and spectres aren't Nephandi. When you're in crossover, if Mages call other groups Nephandi, other game lines' focal characters are probably going to roll their eyes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It has been used to describe that on several occasions. I'll admit that M20 is the one I have least memory of, I read it once but I don't mind using it all too much, since the only thing I really need the books for is to look up some Spheres or the eventual rule, and even that is rare, since I know most of them by memory. But I can tell you that this is used extensively from the 1st Ed to rev, and even in the Sorcerers' Crusade and other supplements. &quot;Nephandi&quot; can be used to talk about the fallen Mages but also about ALL forces of corruption (that is, the Fallens' pawns and also their masters). The way to distinguish between each use is a matter of context. If memory serves, even books that talk about the fallen (like the &quot;Book of Madness&quot; for example) uses the term Nephandi with BOTH meanings - sometimes referring just to the fallen mages, sometimes referring to all forces of corruption, with the difference being left exclusively to the context.<br /> <br /> Granted, I see now how this creates more confusion than it solves, but that's how it is. </div> </div> </div>Even the masters of the Fallen are almost entirely going to be Mage-specific figures with a distinct minority of crossover overlap. Even if you claimed all the Maeljin (which you can't, they're not Mage characters), that would still leave the Triatic Wyrms above them and whatever the Wyrm sees when it looks in the mirror on the rare occasions when its thoughts form a whole Supernal and not a fractured, mangled ego that can't fully realize why things are wrong, only that they are, and is in constant agony to the point where it doesn't even care how it gets free anymore, or if attempts to get free will actually work.<br /> <br /> If you are dealing with Pentex, you are dealing with the above assumption about how the setting works - Mages are wrong about major metaphysical forces being whole and pure, and the universe is, in fact, off-kilter because of &quot;Stasis&quot; captured &quot;Entropy&quot; and now you have to deal with Corruption. This is the very Essence of the WICs and the statement they make about the setting; without it, it won't have any teeth at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-21T12:25:14-08:00","id":1547178,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't it make sense to deal with the most obvious threat to the Tellurian in the Cities? If I were to choose it would be Vampires since the Paradigm doesn't affect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T05:26:37-08:00","id":1547454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546508-next-on-the-technocracy-s-hit-list#post1546508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scenario: The Technocracy has finally WON the Ascension War, definitively! The Council and Disparates are shattered, most of the survivors being taken out or brainwashed; the Marauders and Nephandi have been purged from Creation and chased back out of Reality; and the Crafts are hiding, hoping to avoid notice. After a period of regrouping, replenishing membership and repair, the Order of Reason is stronger than ever!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's weird. Because We Nephandi have actually infiltrated the highest ranks of the Technocracy. Saying you &quot;purged&quot; the nephandi is like saying you purged the sphere's of majik. Qliphothic spheres do not oppose reason and there is no reason, why a member of the Order of Reason would have a problem using them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28682-wednesday-child-of-woe","name":"Wednesday: Child of Woe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28682_1.png","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-15T06:02:19-07:00","id":1549336,"title":"","content":"I have a setting tweak where the Ascension War heated up and expanded to the other supernaturals as the Technocracy started to target them (either out of its own flaws or b/c the Nephandic infiltrators manipulated it). This caused most supernaturals to be reorganized into Triatic uber-factions. It is somewhat similar to what yout describe yet wholly different since the world is engulfed in an Apocalyptic conflict and the Static faction does not seem the strongest one (the Dynamic one is, because the conflict severely weakens the Consensus, Banality, and the Gauntlet). If you think it may be somewhat inspirational to you, it is covered <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415135-the-ascension-war-expands-to-the-other-supernaturals-and-heats-up\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-15-2025, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}